// Quiet Bible: a clear "t" in "water" for voices listed in VoiceBridge.CLEAR_T_VOICES.
// Kristin learned American speech, so she flaps the t in "water" ("wadder") although eSpeak
// gives her a plain t. Secondary stress on the syllable after the t (",") makes her say it.
// Only these forms: in compounds and -eth/-est/-ing forms the stress made the word break apart.
water		w'O:t,3
waters		w'O:t,3z
watered		w'O:t,3d
wateredst	w'O:t,3dst
